@startuml
title NitroCircus - Delivery and Optional Deploy

skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false

actor PO as "Product Owner"
participant BOT as "Telegram Bot"
participant API as "Orchestrator API"
database DB as "MongoDB"
participant GH as "GitHub"
collections FS as "projects/<slug>/"
participant ZIP as "Bundle Builder"
participant DO as "DevOps flow"

== Deliver ==
PO -> BOT : /deliver <project>
BOT -> API : project.deliver
API -> DB : normalize tasks -> done
API -> DB : project -> delivered
API -> GH : issues -> status:done / close
API -> ZIP : export bundle
ZIP -> GH : download main snapshot + task branches
ZIP -> FS : write README/TASKS/RUNBOOK/\nARTIFACTS/.env.example/DELIVERY.json
ZIP -> FS : create <slug>.zip
API -> GH : publish top-level bundle files to main\n(best effort)
API -> DB : log project.delivered
BOT --> PO : entrega completada

== Optional deploy ==
PO -> BOT : /deploy <project>
BOT -> API : project.deploy
API -> DO : queue deploy preparation
DO -> GH : workflows / secrets / pipeline
DO --> PO : solicita IP / usuario / método auth

note right of API
Deliver no implica deploy.
Deploy sigue siendo posterior y explícito.
end note

note right of GH
Si la publicación automática falla,
la entrega no se bloquea.
El warning queda en DELIVERY.json y event logs.
end note

@enduml

